# Commit and push after each phase

When a phase in a technical PRD (`ai-workspace/*_prd.md`) is complete — its tests pass, its acceptance criteria are checked, and its status marker is updated — commit that phase and push it to the remote. Do not wait to be asked. Do not start the next phase in the same turn.

Commit only the files for that phase. Write a message that says why the phase exists, in the repository's existing style. Example:

> Add the questions, choices, and attempts tables.

Push the current branch with `git push`. If it has no upstream yet, use `git push -u origin HEAD`. Never push to `main` or `master`. Never force-push.

If a later request starts the next phase while the finished phase is still uncommitted, commit and push that phase first, then stop.
